<div style="padding:.5em; margin:0">
:This is the documentation for [[Module:BadgeData]].
:For current badge versions, color and image data is managed at [[Module:ObjectData]].
'''Data Structure and Fields'''
<syntaxhighlight lang=lua style="margin: 0">
General = { -- Badges section start
	
{ -- Badge entry start

	-- Exact ingame title
	title = 'Welcome', 
	
	-- Exact ingame text below the title
	text = 'Enjoy your stay!',
	
	-- Exact ingame directions text
	directions = 'Join for the first time.',
	
	-- Extra tutorial for the wiki if needed
	tutorial = 'To get this, go there, do this.', -- or nil
	
	-- If the badge's ingame text, directions, title or image reference anything, add data about it
	references = 'References the hit title "1984" by George Orwell...', -- or nil

	-- List all rewards given upon completing the achievement
	rewards = { -- if there are no rewards, just put nil
		Knob = 100, -- Key = Value
		Stardust = 123,
		Revive = 30,
		'EpicSkin.png|link=items' -- Any images of skins can be added
	},
	
	-- If achievement doesn't count towards progression
	secret = false, -- or true
	
	-- If achievement doesn't show up in the index on a fresh account
	hidden = false, -- or true
	
	-- If achievement is currently obtainable through any means besides being given by developers directly
	obtainable = true, -- or false
	
	-- Exact ID string of the achievement's Roblox badge ID
	id = '2127715318', -- or nil if there is no actual badge

	-- Old achievement versions entries (include if title, text, image or directions were changed)
	-- If the achievement got an entire new badge ID, it is not an old version
	-- Do not add this parameter at all if there are no old versions
	oldVersions = {
	
		{ -- start of old version entry
		
			... -- Contains exact same data as regular entry, minus the oldVersions itself & id
			
			-- Use game files color name, badge color names can be found at [[Achievements/Gradients]]
			color = 'Default v1',
			image = "Epic Badge v1.png"
			
		},  -- end of old version entry
		
		... -- continue adding all old versions
	},
	
}, -- Badge entry end

... -- Continue adding badges falling under this section using exact same entry structure

},  -- Badges section end

... -- continue badge sections
</syntaxhighlight>

</div>

<div class="article-table documentation" style="padding:.5em; border-top:1px solid #5556">The above data is used by [[Module:BadgeList]] to generate badge/achievements lists and related information.
</div>

